==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Unlike the original, this stage has a Cat Limit of 10 while allowing all Cats regardless of rarity. This means that dealing with I.M. Phace is a different kind of challenge.

To begin, the Mooth at the start is no real challenge and can be a major source of money. Take him out quickly with units such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] for that money, as I.M. Phace spawns in rather quickly on a timer. Even with the Cat Limit, stalling and defeating I.M. Phace can still be a challenge. Any Cats with higher range are recommended since the Cat limit and other enemies make stalling I.M. Phace rather difficult. Depending on how long things take, a Zigge, a General GreGory, and another Mooth all spawn in while you are still dealing with I.M. Phace. However, units such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] can still help with all of them, as well as [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]].

==='''Chapter 2'''===
-

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage is even easier in Chapter 3, as the large, ranged threats only spawn much later, the base still has relatively low health given players would have already completed CotC 3 it shouldn't be much of a challenge, since the Cat Limit is higher as well.

It's entirely possible to clear the stage before Zamelle spawns. While little funds are available initially, The Kitty of Liberty is a cheap and powerful response to the UltraBaaBaa that follows soon after. Can Can Cats should be deployed as soon as possible to accumulate DPS and the base will fall in no time.

